  "workflows": {},
  "implementation_policy": "Physics: libuipc CUDA IPC solve (physics/simulate_source.py) of a rigid affine-body medicine ball rolling without slip into the curled end of a yoga mat modelled as one NeoHookean shell with discrete shell bending and the native viscosity extension (plugin assets/scenes/yoga_mat_rolled_edge/native), 97x25 vertices, dt 1/960 s, sampled at t=(i-1)/24 for 96 frames from the accepted settled state (assets settled_state.npz); DELETE mat is the closed-form rigid-floor branch on the CPU; the timed edit restores the source state of its frame (--source-cache/--edit-frame) and continues with the edited value. The simulate entry fills the per-case parameters from edit_vocab.py, launches the solve on a leased GPU (tools/worker_run.py) and audits the cache (physics/audit_source.py). Render: Blender 4.3.2 Cycles replay of the cache (appearance/render_source_review.py) with the published daylight look of appearance/realism.py, 96 samples, 1280x720, encoded at 24 fps. tools/export_ground_truth.py writes pcve_ground_truth/1 from a suite case's native cache and render record; --stage verify checks the published suite against the builder catalog, edit_vocab.py and fresh ground-truth exports. Material values are effective, not calibrated.",
